          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "No. Recall is the read path: it only emits `prior-incidents.md` and writes nothing to the vault. Re-running it on the same ticket just regenerates that artifact.\n\nIf you meant vault-update, that upserts the incident note by ticket id. A re-run updates fields in place, so it never creates a second note for the same ticket.\n\nIf you see a duplicate incident note, something is writing outside the upsert path. Tell me which note it is and I'll look."
