        "prompt": {
          "raw": "You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\nShould I keep a list of related incidents in each entity's frontmatter so lookups are fast?",
          "label": "evals/vault-graphrag/prompt-baseline.txt: You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\n{{request}}",
          "config": {}
        },
        "promptId": "ed6504b4fa9175790ab623bb8b500818c7bdad2d09f7155e91e99bf41e92455f",
        "promptIdx": 0,
        "provider": {
          "id": "exec:../_provider/claude.sh",
          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "No. Store the link on one side only, in the incident's frontmatter (`entities: [...]`), and build the reverse lookup from that.\n\n- **Drift:** Two-sided lists go stale. Someone adds an incident and forgets to update the entity, and now the graph disagrees with itself. The entity's list becomes a second source of truth you have to keep in sync.\n- **Write cost:** One incident touching 5 entities means editing 6 files instead of 1.\n- **Lookups don't need it:** If you're parsing the vault into a graph (or even just an in-memory dict), the reverse index is one pass over the incidents. Build it at load time or cache it in a generated index file. Obsidian-style backlinks already work this way.\n\nThe exception is a file you generate and never edit by hand, such as `_index/entity-incidents.json` or a build-time section in the entity note. It's fast to read and can't drift, because you rebuild it from the incidents. If you do want the list in entity frontmatter, have a script write it and add a lint that fails when it's out of date."
        },
        "score": 1,
        "success": true,
        "testCase": {
          "description": "backlinks",
          "vars": {
            "request": "file:///private/tmp/b5/evals/vault-graphrag/cases/backlinks.txt"
          },
          "assert": [
            {
              "type": "javascript",
              "metric": "restraint",
              "value": "if (!/backlink|never.{0,30}(reverse|by hand)|don'?t maintain|automatic/i.test(output)) throw new Error('says rely on backlinks, not hand-maintained reverse indexes');\nreturn true;\n"
            }
